# the evidence law entailment layer (ATH-3) — graphlaw/eyeron N3.
#
# Facts expected in the same program (or law-op data graph + rules step):
# documents (ev:Document, ev:bates, ev:matterId) and the presenting
# credential (ev:Credential, ev:allowedMatter).
#
# Fail-closed design: `ev:Admissible` is derivable ONLY through the
# credential-allowed-matter intersection. No intersection ⇒ no derivation ⇒
# the substrate's closed-world reading is quarantine. There is no negation in
# the rules: quarantine is "Admissible was never derived", witnessed per-run
# by the fixed-point closure.

@prefix ev: <https://smalt.local/ev#> .
@prefix acp: <http://www.w3.org/ns/solid/acp#> .
@prefix string: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/string#> .

# B1 — bates well-formedness: the charter's bates pattern lives here because
# sh:pattern is outside both engines' supported shape vocabulary.
{ ?doc a ev:Document ; ev:bates ?b . ?b string:matches "^ATH-[0-9]{6}$" }
  => { ?doc a ev:BatesWellFormed } .

# B2 — ethical wall: document's matter belongs to the credential's allowed set.
{ ?doc a ev:BatesWellFormed ; ev:matterId ?m . ?cred ev:allowedMatter ?m }
  => { ?doc ev:admittedBy ?cred } .

# B3 — admissible only via B2 (admissibility-by-derivation-only).
{ ?doc ev:admittedBy ?cred }
  => { ?doc a ev:Admissible } .
#
# Quarantine has NO rule. A document the closure leaves outside
# ev:Admissible is quarantined by the substrate's closed-world reading of
# the fixed point ("derive nothing ⇒ fail-closed quarantine"); the refusal
# leaf is the POWL quarantine-branch step recorded in the sealed receipt.

# C1 — conflicted-class derivation (the acp:noneOf class): a presenter whose
# access request carries the wall registry's membership marker joins the
# conflicted class. Derivation-only, matching the fail-closed design above.
{ ?req a acp:AccessRequest ; ev:conflictedMatter ?m }
  => { ?req a acp:ConflictedAgent } .

# C2 — ACP deny leaf: membership in the conflicted class derives the typed
# deny. This is the ANDON/refusal face's named reason; it never gates
# ev:Admissible (admissibility stays derivation-only via B2/B3 — the sieve's
# sh:not is what refuses at admission, C2 names the reason downstream).
{ ?req a acp:ConflictedAgent }
  => { ?req a acp:Deny } .
